---
description: Actually Deals product and architecture rules
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `BLUEPRINT.md` as the source of truth, then `docs/CONSTITUTION.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/DATABASE.md`.

- Persist deals, votes, and comments only through `src/lib/store.ts`.
- Never use `next/image` for product photos. Use a standard `<img>` with the 3-tier resolver in `src/lib/images.ts`.
- `/api/parse-deal` must stay merchant-tolerant: extract IDs from the URL even when the retailer blocks the scrape.
- Strip tracking params and attach affiliate tags in `src/lib/affiliate.ts`. Do not leave `utm_*`, `pf_rd_*`, or click IDs on outbound links.
- Amazon Associates Store ID is `actuallydea07-20` (`NEXT_PUBLIC_AMAZON_AFFILIATE_TAG` / `AFFILIATE_AMAZON_TAG`). Do not use `actuallydeals-20`.
- Deal cards stay fully clickable without breaking nested Copy Code / Get Deal controls.
- Do not add auth providers, extra component libraries, or a second database.
- After behavior changes, keep `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` green.
- House social: X `@actuallydeals`, Instagram `actuallydeals_` (underscore; URL `https://www.instagram.com/actuallydeals_/`), Facebook `ActuallyDeals`. Do not drop the Instagram underscore. Do not change the X handle or the domain `actuallydeals.com`. Use `src/lib/social.ts`.
